From 6204b6ee2785526af7c71a5be83afecdef79e886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:45:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 752/752] SableOS: Contacts list with A-Z rail, letter keys and
 numbers

Ports the approved SableOS Contacts presentation to LineageOS Contacts:

* One alphabet rail: an A-Z rail at the end edge of the list reads the
  adapter's existing section indexer (ListView header views counted);
  letters without contacts are dimmed and skipped by focus. While it
  shows, the upstream fast-scroll thumb is off so there is one rail; it
  hides in search mode.
* Physical keyboard (CONTACTS_PEOPLE_UX): with search closed a letter
  key moves the list selection to the first contact under that letter
  and repeating it cycles; with no match the selection stays and "No
  contacts under X" is shown; "/" opens an empty search. Letters never
  open, call, message or edit anyone. Ctrl/Alt/Meta combinations and
  every other character keep the upstream type-to-search, and nothing
  changes in search or selection mode.
* Local-directory rows show the contact's default number with its type
  label under the name, from one read-only ContactsProvider Phone query
  reduced off the main thread into the bounded SablePreferredNumbers
  map; it reloads on provider changes and writes nothing.
* Section letters are larger and lighter (22sp, light, not all caps)
  and the people toolbar is flat. Colours keep following the system
  palette, which the Sable accent drives.

ContactsProvider stays the owner of contact data; accounts, sync,
permissions, linking and editing are unchanged. No second index or
database is added.
